    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0958" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg862"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carbo to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Ecuador</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                            York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-06-24"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June 24, 1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Having brought to the knowledge
                    of my Government the contents of the various communications which your
                    Department has addressed to me relative to the state of war which exists between
                    the United States of America and the Kingdom of Spain, I have received
                    instructions to state to you that the Government of Ecuador, while deploring the
                    armed contest between two powers with which it maintains relations of good
                    friendship and commerce, declares its absolute neutrality in accordance with the
                    law of nations.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">L. F. Carbo.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
